#Description
#tSNE (t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding) is a type of unsupervised learning algorithm that is used for dimensionality reduction. It works by finding the k t-distributed neighbors of the data and using them to represent the data in a lower-dimensional space. It is useful for visualizing high-dimensional data in a 2D or 3D space. Each t-distributed neighbor is defined by its distance (euclidean distance) and its importance (probability). The algorithm iteratively updates the t-distributed neighbors until the data is well-represented in the lower-dimensional space.
